cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Moby-DIC in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Moby-DIC: 2D digital image correlation for mechanical testing"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "João Felipe"
    family-names: "Queiroz Rodrigues"
    affiliation: "Universidade Estadual de Campinas (UNICAMP)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jfunicamp/Moby-DIC"
url: "https://github.com/jfunicamp/Moby-DIC"
abstract: >-
  Moby-DIC measures full-field displacements and strains on a specimen surface from the
  image sequence or video of a mechanical test, using local subset digital image correlation
  (IC-GN, ZNSSD, affine subsets, cubic B-spline interpolation). It synchronises the images with
  the tensile machine curve, provides a digital extensometer and writes a self-contained
  interactive viewer for every result. Guided interface in English and Portuguese.
version: "1.3.1"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - digital image correlation
  - DIC
  - full-field strain measurement
  - experimental mechanics
  - mechanical testing
